# The annotations of REX 1, the game's part 1 (the code block $6018-$FFF9 of Side 1): the single source of truth for
# src/game/*.asm (kit/mkgame.py --case .). REX 2 (src/rex2/rex2.ann) and the DEMO (src/demo/demo.ann) are the same
# engine built again at other addresses; their names follow these.
#
#   @module NAME ; title            the entries from here on go to NAME.asm, the title heads the file
#   @about a paragraph              the module file's header text, one paragraph a line
#   $ADDR c Name ; title            a routine
#   > a description line
#   $ADDR b Name ; title            data (w words, t text, s space; "b Name 8" rows of 8)
#   @res graphics/NAME.bin          the entry is a resource: src/res/..., INCBIN
#   $ADDR Name ; comment            a label and comment inside an entry
#   (var) ADDR NAME [N]             a variable inside the work space at $A012 (the @var directive)
#   (inline) ADDR N                 a routine that reads N data bytes after the CALL
#
# Witness lines give the runs of the entry's first instruction over the stage 1 recordings (case.json read_builds:
# c1, the tape load into the menu and a game, and the 33 RZX segments of part 1, rzx-p1-*); --fix-witness keeps them.

@inline $D8C0 6

@alias ShadowOffset $E4FF-$5800 ; the distance from a screen attribute to its cell in the attribute shadow $E4FF (PowerBar adds it); not an address in the sprites
@isub $B97A LD DE,ShadowOffset
@isub $BA26 LD DE,ShadowOffset

@module graphics ; The graphics and the level data: the font, the characters, the blocks, the room maps and the sprites
@about The tape loads the code block at $6018 (CLEAR 24599). Its first bytes are a leftover of the authors' development link (DevLinkStub $6018-$607D); the menu copies the object explosion picture from $E336 over it (192 bytes, $6018-$60D7), so the stub never runs. Then come the tables every room is built from: the 64-character font (Font $60E0, characters 32-95, found at $5FE0 + 8 x code), a flag byte for each of the 256 room characters (CharFlags $62E0: the cell types Rex and the objects test), the 256 characters (CharGraphics $63E0, 8 bytes each), their attributes (CharAttrs $6BE0), the 256 blocks of 3 x 3 characters (BlockDefs $6CE0) and the rooms (RoomMaps $75E0, 7 rows of 10 blocks, 70 bytes a room).
@about The sprites follow from $7F72 to $9479. Each is stored pre-shifted: a frame list of 8 offsets (ShiftFrames $AE5D and the like, one an X & 7) picks the copy for the pixel phase, and DrawSprite $B258 ORs it into the back buffer, width and height from $A0B1 / $A0B2. Their owners are named at each label.
$6018 b DevLinkStub 16 ; Leftover: 102 bytes of the authors' development link, overwritten by the menu before they could run
> No instruction jumps here. The menu (TitleMenu $DAC0) copies ExplosionPicture $E336 to $6018 (192 bytes) before anything else, and the objects use $6018 as the explosion picture from then on (UpdateObject $BA86). Kept byte for byte as a documented leftover (src/res/leftovers/README.md).
@res leftovers/rex1-devlink.bin
$607E b Unused607E 16 ; Leftover: 98 bytes after the stub (overwritten by the explosion picture up to $60D7); nothing reads them before
@res leftovers/rex1-devlink.bin
$60E0 b Font 8 ; The font: 64 characters, codes 32-95 (space to underscore), 8 bytes each, at $5FE0 + 8 x code
> PrintChar $A2E9, PrintDigits $A3C8, the box frame of PanelBox $CE7B and the DEFINE key echo (FontChar $DEF0) read it. The box frame uses six characters as corner and edge pieces ($6120 "(", $6130 "*", $6140 ",", $6158 "/", $61B8 ";", $61C8 "=").
@res fonts/rex1.bin
$62E0 b CharFlags 16 ; The cell type of each of the 256 room characters: what Rex and the objects test in the room grid
> DrawRoomCell $C7E2 copies CharFlags[c] into the grid $E1FF for each character drawn. The values tested: 0 empty, 2, 4, 5, 6 solid (SolidCells $D096), $07 the restart marker, $08 the shield recharger, $0A-$0D the weapon stations, $0E-$12 solid platform kinds, $12 the ladder or lift (CellsUnderRex $9F5F).
@res tables/rex1-char-flags.bin
$63E0 b CharGraphics 8 ; The 256 room characters, 8 bytes each
> Drawn by DrawRoomCell $C7E2 into the back buffer; the animated ones are rotated in place each pass by the main loop ($6438, $64B0, $64C0, $6600, $6758, $67D8, $6858, $6BA8, $6BB0, $6BC0).
@res chars/rex1.bin
$6438 AnimChar11 ; character 11, rolled one line up by RollCharUp $A7A9 every pass (MainAnimate)
$64B0 AnimChar26 ; character 26, rolled one line down by RollCharDown $A7BA
$64C0 AnimChar28 ; character 28, rolled one line down by RollCharDown
$6600 AnimChar68 ; character 68: frames from FramesList1 $A60C (AnimateCells $A55E, CopyFrame)
$6758 AnimChar111 ; character 111: each line rotated right (RRC) by the main loop
$67D8 AnimChar127 ; character 127: frames from FramesList4 $A61A (CopyFrame)
$6858 AnimChar143 ; character 143: each line rotated left (RLC)
$6BA8 AnimChar249 ; character 249: frames from FramesList3 $A5F4 (AnimateRestart $A5B7)
$6BB0 AnimChar250 ; character 250: frames from FramesList2 $A602 (AnimateCells2 $A5A7)
$6BC0 AnimChar252 ; characters 252-255: AnimFramesA $AE8D / AnimFramesB $AEAD on alternate passes (AnimateCells)
$6BE0 b CharAttrs 16 ; The attribute of each of the 256 room characters
@res chars/rex1.bin
$6CE0 b BlockDefs 9 ; The 256 blocks: 3 x 3 character codes each, rows top to bottom
@res blocks/rex1.bin
$75E0 b RoomMaps 10 ; The rooms 0-34: 7 rows of 10 block codes each (70 bytes a room); room n at $75E0 + 70n
> DrawRoom $C745 builds the room in the grid and the back buffer from here. A room is 30 x 21 characters.
@res rooms/rex1-maps.bin
$7F72 b Sprites 16 ; The sprites, pre-shifted: each label is a picture set its owner draws through a frame list
> $7F72 is the foot man (kind 0) and UpdateObject's default picture. The labels below name the other owners.
@res sprites/rex1.bin
$8032 SpriteStomper ; kind 1 (stomper)
$80F2 SpriteRex ; Rex walking (DrawRex $96A7)
$816A SpriteRexDeath ; the base of Rex's death shards (DeathAnimation $9AC5: frame n at +72 n, n 1-8, so SpritePoints' frames; these 72 bytes are never drawn)
$81B2 SpritePoints ; the points sign a kill leaves (ShowPoints $97FD)
$83F2 SpriteKind5 ; kind 5
$84B2 SpriteKind3 ; kind 3
$8572 SpriteKind4 ; kind 4
$8632 SpriteHitFlash ; an object hit (HitObject $D3C2, HitObjectHard $D41F)
$8692 SpriteRamTurn ; the hit foot man turning (RamTurn $BD44)
$86F2 SpritePodA ; a pod left by an explosion ($BDED)
$87B2 SpritePodB ; a pod left by an explosion ($BE18)
$8872 SpritePowerPod ; the power pod's four frames ($8872, $8892, $88B2, $88D2: AnimatePod $BED3)
$88F2 SpriteShield ; the shield bubble round Rex, 4 x 21, through ShiftFrames2 (DrawShield $9726)
$8A42 SpriteLaserA ; the laser beam fired left: 6 frames of 4 bytes, copied by BeamByte $B852 ($B849)
$8A5A SpriteScanner ; kind 8 (scanner) ($C3B0, $C3D2)
$8B5A SpriteScanner2 ; kind 8's start picture (InitKind8 $CCBF)
$8C0A SpriteHudIcons ; the HUD's weapon and bomb icons (DrawHudIcons $A1E2)
$8CAA SpriteHudIcons2 ; the HUD's weapon icons, second row (DrawWeaponIcon $A21F)
$8CEA SpriteBonusPod ; the bonus pod (kind $7D, $BE39)
$8D0A SpriteBonusPod2 ; ($BE43)
$8D8A SpriteKind12 ; kind 12 (ramming pod)
$8E4A SpriteKind11 ; kind 11 (launcher)
$8E6A SpriteKind10 ; kind 10 (shooters)
$8E8A SpriteKind6 ; kind 6
$8EAA SpriteSwingGun ; kind 9 (swing gun), its angles (SwingGunFrames $BECB)
$8F4A SpriteLaserB ; the laser beam fired right: 6 frames of 4 bytes, copied by BeamByte $B852 ($B83F)
$8F62 SpriteRexJump ; Rex jumping or falling, off a lift (DrawRex $96C4)
$9022 SpriteKind15 ; kind 15 (blob)
$90A2 SpriteKind13 ; kind 13 (mine layer)
$9132 SpriteKind14 ; kind 14 (mine)
$91B2 SpriteJumper ; the jumping walkers ($C5AB)
$91D2 SpriteKind16 ; kind 16 (the big gun)
$92F2 SpriteHuman ; a human killed ($98C1)

@module entry ; The entry, a new game, the waits for fire
@about The BASIC's RANDOMIZE USR 38010 lands at GameEntry: interrupts off for good (the game never waits for a frame: one pass of the main loop is as long as its work), the title and menu (TitleMenu $DAC0), then the high score 10 and NewGame. NewGame resets every variable (4 lives, 3 smart bombs, shield 99), clears the screen, draws the HUD, prints PHASE ONE and PRESS FIRE TO BEGIN and waits for fire after each; only the second wait's result is tested, so the attract mode (Attract $A915) starts when both run out (2 x 50000 polls, about 14 s). Rex then materialises in room 0 and the main loop runs.
$947A c GameEntry ; The code block's entry (USR 38010): DI, the menu, the high score, then NewGame
> Clears ControlXor $A0AE (keys, not Kempston) and AttractFlag $A0C2, calls TitleMenu $DAC0, clears the attribute shadow $E4FF-$E7FE (the title screen's bytes, no longer needed) and sets HiScore $A08B = 10. Falls into NewGame.
> Witness: L1 1 (c1).
$9498 c NewGame ; A new game: every variable reset, the HUD, PHASE ONE and PRESS FIRE TO BEGIN, the wait for fire, Rex materialises
> Also the target of ENTER in the main loop (restart), of the game over and of the attract mode. InitDrones $A628; border black; Lives $A063 = 4, Bombs $A06C = 3, ResetPower $BA49, ShieldEnergy $A04D = 99, the weapons held $A050-$A053 = 0, the score, HumansKilled $A089 and the extra life count 0, the random seeds $A0A1 = $0313, $A0A3 = $11; Rex at X $A0, Y $60 in room 0 facing right, the restart point the same. Then ClearScreen $A3AE, DrawHud $A1A5, ShowLives $99BB, SaveAttrs $CF8F, the texts PhaseOneText $AAAE and PressFireText $AB25 (PrintBoxed $A13E) each followed by WaitFireOrAttract $97C3; SoundReset $D5AE and Materialise $9D1F. Falls into MainLoop.
> Witness: L1 9 (c1, p1-code, p1-cursor, p1-define, p1-kempston, rzx-p1-00000, rzx-p1-64000).

@module mainloop ; The main loop: one pass a frame of play, the keys
@about MainLoop builds the current room (BuildRoom $A89D) and loops at MainPass $9586. A pass moves the bullets (MoveBullets $B64E, MoveEnemyBullets $B645), the drones (UpdateDrones $A639), Rex's death or sparkle (RexState $969B, SparkleUpdate $9D71, SparkleDraw $9E02), the objects (UpdateObjects $BA5C), the sound (SoundStep $D68C, twice), draws the animated cells (DrawAnimCells $B33E), copies the back buffer to the screen (BufferToScreen $A28A) and clears it (ClearBuffer $B205), then the collisions (EnemyBulletsHitRex $D1B9), the power bar (PowerBar $B96B), the spawners (SpawnScripted $C978, SpawnRandom $C9CA), the smart bomb (SmartBombStep $9786), the kill flash (KillFlashFade $9992), the fade (FadeStep $9A4C) and the HUD sweep (HudSweep $A0C4).
@about Then the keys: down toggles the shield, ENTER restarts (NewGame), H pauses, SPACE fires a smart bomb; while Rex lives, fire, right, left and up (jump), then the jump, the fall and the walk, and the cells under Rex. Last the animated characters are rotated. There is no frame wait: interrupts stay off, so the game's speed is its work.
$9583 c MainLoop ; Build the room, then one pass of play a frame (MainPass)
> The room change (ChangeRoom $C95A) and the life lost jump back here. The keys are the readers $A477-$A4DB: down ShieldToggle $967F, fire FireWeapon $B372, right WalkRight $CFDA, left WalkLeft $CFF6, up StartJump $D0C2; ENTER ($BFFE bit 0) NewGame, H ($BFFE bit 4) Pause $A4E7, SPACE ($7FFE bit 0) SmartBomb $9751. ENTER, H and SPACE are fixed keys; the other five follow the menu's choice (DEFINE, Kempston, Cursor, Sinclair).
> Witness: L1 79 (c1, p1-cursor, p1-define, p1-kempston, p1-rooms238, p1-speedup, p1-room x5, rzx-p1- x30).
$9586 MainPass ; one pass: bullets, drones, Rex, objects, sound, draw, collisions, HUD
$95D2 MainKeys ; the fixed keys: ENTER, H, SPACE
$9617 MainRexKeys ; while Rex lives: fire
$9627 MainRight ; right
$9645 MainAnimate ; the animated characters: RRC, RLC, rolls
$964A MainRrcLoop ; rotate each line of character 111 right
$9654 MainRlcLoop ; rotate each line of character 143 left
$967B c SoundOffReturn ; CALL SoundSilence: RET; no instruction reaches it (leftover)
> Four bytes between the main loop's JP and ShieldToggle. No jump or call names $967B (known only from the code).
> Witness: L1 0 ().

@module rex ; Rex: the shield, his state and his picture
@about Rex is a sprite at RexX $A0B6 / RexY $A0B7 (pixels; the play area starts at line 24) facing RexFacing $A0BB. The down key toggles the shield (ShieldOn $A049), which drains ShieldEnergy $A04D while on and stops shots and enemies (EnemyBulletsHitRex $D1B9, ObjectHitsRex $D215 test it). RexState runs the death animation while Dying $A055 is set; DrawRex picks his picture: walking, jumping or shielded.
$967F c ShieldToggle ; The down key: switch the shield on or off (once a press, only with energy left)
> Called by MainPass when ReadDown $A4DB sees the key. ShieldKeyLatch $A04C keeps it to one toggle a press; the shield goes on only while ShieldEnergy $A04D is not 0 and Rex is not materialising ($A060).
> Witness: L1 299 (c1, p1-code, p1-cursor, p1-define, p1-kempston, p1-speedup, p1-room30, rzx-p1- x32).
$969B c RexState ; Rex's death animation while he is present and Dying $A055 is set, else nothing
> Returns while Rex is not present (RexPresent $A05D 0: he is materialising); then, if Dying $A055, JP DeathAnimation $9AC5. Called every pass.
> Witness: L1 18528 (c1, p1-code, p1-cursor, p1-define, p1-gameover, p1-kempston, p1-poke41241, p1-rooms238, p1-shots, p1-speedup, p1-room x5, rzx-p1- x32).
$96A7 c DrawRex ; Draw Rex: his picture (walking or jumping); with the shield on, its hum, its drain and the bubble
> Sets SpriteX $A0AF, SpriteY $A0B0, the size 3 x 16 ($A0B1, $A0B2) and the mirror flag by RexFacing; the picture through ShiftFrames $AE5D: SpriteRexJump $8F62 while jumping or falling (and not on a lift, OnLift $A07A), else SpriteRex $80F2. DrawSprite $B258. With ShieldOn $A049: the hum SfxShield (its period SfxShieldTone = $04B0 + Random & $1F) started when channel 2 is free, ShieldDrain $99D3 with L = 1, then the bubble SpriteShield $88F2, 4 x 21, through ShiftFrames2 $AE65, 4 pixels left of Rex (8 right of that facing left) and 2 lines up.
> Witness: L1 17095 (c1, p1-code, p1-cursor, p1-define, p1-gameover, p1-kempston, p1-poke41241, p1-rooms238, p1-shots, p1-speedup, p1-room x5, rzx-p1- x32).
$96DC DrawRexWalk ; on a lift or on the ground: the walking picture
$96E2 DrawRexFacing ; the mirror flag by facing
$970A DrawRexShield ; the shield on: drain it, the bubble's X
$9726 DrawShield ; the bubble, 4 x 21 from two lines above Rex

@module bomb ; The smart bomb
@about SPACE fires a smart bomb (Bombs $A06C, 3 at the start, more from bomb pods): SmartBomb takes one, SmartBombMark stops every enemy bullet, and SmartBombStep kills the object records one a pass over 16 steps ($A02F); there is no screen flash of its own (each kill flashes its cells, CopyAttrs restores the colours at the end). A life lost fires one for free (SmartBombFree $9749 from RexDies $9BDA), so the room is empty when Rex comes back.
$9749 c SmartBombFree ; A smart bomb that costs nothing (Rex's death): unless one is running, mark the room's objects
> Witness: L1 42 (c1, p1-cursor, p1-define, p1-gameover, p1-kempston, p1-room24, p1-room30, rzx-p1- x18).
$9751 c SmartBomb ; SPACE: one smart bomb from Bombs $A06C (none left, nothing), the HUD updated, the room's objects marked
> Witness: L1 15 (c1, p1-cursor, rzx-p1- x5).
$9763 c SmartBombMark ; Start the smart bomb: SmartBombOn $A030 = 1, 16 steps, SmartBombPtr $5E66; every enemy bullet stopped (the live byte +6 of the 20 records from $5D22 set to 2)
> Writes the object pointers from ObjectTable $5E66 (ObjectCount $A092 records of 24 bytes) into the list at $5D28.
> Witness: L1 50 (c1, p1-cursor, p1-define, p1-gameover, p1-kempston, p1-room24, p1-room30, rzx-p1- x22).
$9778 MarkLoop ; the next enemy bullet's live byte
$977F MarkNext ; the next enemy bullet record
$9786 c SmartBombStep ; One step of a running smart bomb: KillObject on the next object record (not kinds $FE, $FD, $FC, $90; neither the alive byte nor kind $FF tested); CopyAttrs after the last step
> Every pass; returns at once while SmartBombOn $A030 is 0. Each step KillObject $981F on the next record; after 16 steps the bomb ends with CopyAttrs $C8BF. A record that died in this room keeps its Y and kind, so it is killed and scored again (a spent explosion: KillScores[15], 200).
> Witness: L1 18501 (c1, p1-code, p1-cursor, p1-define, p1-gameover, p1-kempston, p1-poke41241, p1-rooms238, p1-shots, p1-speedup, p1-room x5, rzx-p1- x32).
$97A9 BombNextObject ; the next marked object

@module entry
$97C3 c WaitFireOrAttract ; Wait up to 50000 polls for fire: Temp1 = 1 after a press and its release, 0 when the count runs out
> Temp1 = 0 and the sound silenced, then DE = 50000 counted down, a DJNZ delay of 30 before each poll of ReadFire $A477. A press: wait for its release (WaitFireRelease), SoundReset $D5AE, Temp1 = 1, RET. The count out: RET with Temp1 0 and the sound still off. NewGame's second call tests Temp1 and jumps to Attract $A915 on 0; the weapon panel (WeaponPanel) ignores it.
> Witness: L1 20 (c1, p1-code, p1-cursor, p1-define, p1-kempston, rzx-p1- x5).
$97CD WaitFireCount ; the 50000-poll count
$97D3 WaitFireDelay ; a short delay between polls
$97DB WaitFireRelease ; fire must be released first
@isub $97CA LD DE,50000
$97EA c WaitFire ; Wait for fire, then for its release (no timeout): after the game over and the CODE panel
> Witness: L1 3 (c1, p1-code, p1-gameover).
$97ED WaitFireDown ; wait for fire pressed
$97F3 WaitFireUp ; wait for fire released

@module score ; The kills, the score, the lives and the shield figure
@about A killed object (KillObject $981F, from a bullet, the smart bomb, a collision or a fall) scores KillScores $994E[kind] x 100 points (AddScore $9A27), turns into the points sign (ShowPoints $97FD) and, for the six kinds that are people (0 foot man, 4, 5, 6, 7 and 12), adds one to HumansKilled $A089 (KillHuman $98A7). The big gun ($90) goes to KillScore $98AF instead: 1000 points and two lives. The game over panel prints HumansKilled. Every 100 x 100 points (ExtraLifeCount $A076) gives a life, at most 9.
$97FD c ShowPoints ; Turn the object at IX into the points sign: picture SpritePoints $81B2, kind $FF (no collisions), at rest
> Witness: L1 5 (rzx-p1-24000).
$981F c KillObject ; Kill the object at IX: its score, the kill flash in the HUD, the explosion sound; people add to HumansKilled
> The kill flash: KillFlashPtr $A039 = the next cell of the HUD's combo row ($5843 + 3 a hit, at rest $E9FF), timer $A03C. Kind 14 (the mine) scores nothing. Kind 5 also ends the scripted spawn (EndScriptSpawn $9968). Then KillHuman $98A7 or ShowPoints $97FD.
> Witness: L1 1016 (c1, p1-code, p1-cursor, p1-define, p1-gameover, p1-kempston, p1-shots, p1-speedup, p1-room24, p1-room30, rzx-p1- x32).
$98A7 c KillHuman ; A person killed: HumansKilled $A089 + 1, nothing else
> For kinds 0, 7, 6, 12, 4 and 5 (KillObject calls it for each). The big gun's KillScore $98AF follows it in memory.
> Witness: L1 155 (c1, p1-speedup, p1-room24, p1-room30, rzx-p1- x27).
$98AF KillScore ; the big gun ($90): 1000 points, hits by weapon, speed 1, the human picture; the second kill makes it a ramming pod (kind $0C, 8 hits); five points signs each time
$990A KillHumanMake ; five points signs in free records around the big gun (FindFreeObject $D858, ShowPoints $97FD): X + Random & 31, Y + Random & 31; pod $FF on the first kill, else Random & 1
$990E KillHumanSet ; its picture and size
$9928 KillHumanLive ; alive
$994E b KillScores 16 ; The score of each object kind, in hundreds: kind 0 1, 1 2, 2 1, 3 1, 4 2, 5 3, 6 1, 7 1, 8 6, 9 6, 10 5, 11 8, 12 3, 13 10, 14 0, 15 2, then 1s
> The menu's roll call agrees: FOOT MAN 100, STOMPER 200, SCANNER 600, SWING GUN 600, SHOOTERS 500, LAUNCHER 800, RAMMING POD 300, MINE LAYER 1000, MINE no score, BLOB 200.
@res tables/rex1-kill-scores.bin
$9968 c EndScriptSpawn ; Stop the scripted spawn (KillObject on a kind 5): the objects of kinds 3 and 4 lose their timer ($9989)
> Witness: L1 2 (rzx-p1-04000, rzx-p1-12000).
$9972 EndSpawnLoop ; each object
$9989 c StopObjectSpawn ; IY's object: timer (IY+$10) = 0, ScriptSpawnStep $A045 = 0
> Witness: L1 10 (rzx-p1-04000, rzx-p1-12000).
$9992 c KillFlashFade ; Fade the HUD's kill flash one step (attribute row $5840, 30 cells), then mark the latest kill's two cells white
> Witness: L1 18613 (c1, p1-code, p1-cursor, p1-define, p1-gameover, p1-kempston, p1-poke41241, p1-rooms238, p1-shots, p1-speedup, p1-room x5, rzx-p1- x32).
$9997 FadeHudLoop ; each HUD attribute one step darker
$999F FadeHudNext ; the next cell
$99AB c ShowScore ; Print Score $A03E in the HUD
> Witness: L1 306 (c1, p1-code, p1-shots, p1-speedup, p1-room30, rzx-p1- x31).
$99BB c ShowLives ; Print Lives $A063 in the HUD
> Witness: L1 53 (c1, p1-code, p1-cursor, p1-define, p1-kempston, p1-room24, p1-room30, rzx-p1- x26).
$99CE c ShieldDrainFast ; ShieldDrainRate $A04E - 1: a hit on the shield drains it faster (EnemyBulletsHitRex, ObjectHitsRex)
> Witness: L1 82 (p1-speedup, p1-room30, rzx-p1- x21).
$99D3 c ShieldDrain ; With the shield on, count ShieldDrainRate down; at 0 one unit of ShieldEnergy $A04D goes; none left switches the shield off
> Witness: L1 2797 (p1-code, p1-cursor, p1-define, p1-kempston, p1-speedup, p1-room26, p1-room30, rzx-p1- x29).
$99EF ShieldOff ; no energy: the shield off
$99FA c ShowShield ; Print ShieldEnergy $A04D in the HUD and colour it: red when low, green otherwise ($E513, $E514 in the attribute shadow)
> Witness: L1 1498 (c1, p1-code, p1-cursor, p1-define, p1-kempston, p1-rooms238, p1-speedup, p1-room x5, rzx-p1- x32).
$9A27 c AddScore ; Score $A03E + HL; every 100 points ExtraLifeCount $A076 counts, at 100 an extra life (ExtraLife $D5A0)
> Not while Rex is dying. Jumps to ShowScore.
> Witness: L1 449 (c1, p1-code, p1-cursor, p1-define, p1-gameover, p1-kempston, p1-shots, p1-speedup, p1-room24, p1-room30, rzx-p1- x32).
$9A49 AddScoreShow ; print it
$9A4C c FadeStep ; The HUD flash of a power pod (only TakePowerPod starts it): rows 0-1 ($5800-$583F) stepped through FadeSteps $9AB3 by FadeStepIndex $A042
> Witness: L1 18613 (c1, p1-code, p1-cursor, p1-define, p1-gameover, p1-kempston, p1-poke41241, p1-rooms238, p1-shots, p1-speedup, p1-room x5, rzx-p1- x32).
$9A65 FadeStepAttr ; the step's attribute change
$9A70 FadeCells ; each cell of the shadow
$9A81 FadeNextCell ; the next cell
$9A8D FadeCopy ; the shadow to the screen
$9A9A FadeIncrease ; a brighter step
$9AA7 FadeDecrease ; a darker step
$9AB3 b FadeSteps 18 ; The fade's 17 steps: 1 six times, 0 five times, 2 six times, then $FF (the end)

@module death ; Rex's death, the life lost, the game over, the restart points, the sparkle
@about RexDies starts a death (not while Immune $A071): Dying $A055 = 1, a free smart bomb, LosePower, ShieldEnergy back to 99, the shield off, the sparkle out (Dematerialise $9D47). DeathAnimation runs 50 passes ($A056) of shards flying from Rex (DeathShards $9C05), then LifeLost: one life less, Rex back at the last restart point (RestartX $A059, RestartY $A05A, RestartRoom $A05B, saved by the restart markers, SaveRestart $9C3B) with a materialise sparkle, and the room built again. No life left: the game over panel (GAME OVER, HI-SCORE, HUMANS KILLED) and a new game.
@about The sparkle ($9D0F-$9F0B) is Rex appearing or vanishing as random dots: SparkleUpdate works on Rex's 3-byte-wide box in the back buffer (SparkleBufferOrigin $E89F): SparkleCount lines cleared, the next 3 lines ANDed with random bytes, SparkleDraw draws the particles (SparkleMasks $9F0C, SparkleDots $9F14).
$9AC5 c DeathAnimation ; One pass of Rex's death: the shards, the death picture, the sound; at the end LifeLost
> The shards follow DeathShards $9C05 (DeathShardPtr $A057 moved by ShardNext $9BC8 / ShardBack $9BD1); SpriteRexDeath $816A; the attribute fade SaveCellAttrs $CF9B / RestoreCellAttrs $CF6E. After DeathTimer $A056 passes: JP LifeLost $9C76.
> Witness: L1 758 (c1, p1-cursor, p1-define, p1-gameover, p1-kempston, p1-room24, p1-room30, rzx-p1- x18).
$9AD2 ShardLoop ; each shard
$9B3A ShardNextRecord ; the next shard
$9B62 DeathTimerStep ; the death's timer
$9BB3 DeathFlash ; a random attribute flash
$9BC8 c ShardNext ; DeathShardPtr $A057 + 2
> Witness: L1 4 (c1, p1-gameover).
$9BD1 c ShardBack ; DeathShardPtr $A057 - 2: the shards step back
> Witness: L1 4 (c1, p1-gameover).
$9BDA c RexDies ; Rex is killed (unless Immune $A071): the sweep reset (ResetSweep), Dying, the timer 50, the free smart bomb, LosePower, ShieldEnergy refilled to 99, dematerialise (which switches the shield off)
> Called by the collisions (EnemyBulletsHitRex $D1B9, ObjectHitsRex $D215), the fall (RexFall $D14D) and the HUD sweep's end (HudSweep $A0C4). Resets the sweep (ResetSweep $A133).
> Witness: L1 221 (c1, p1-cursor, p1-define, p1-gameover, p1-kempston, p1-poke41241, p1-rooms238, p1-speedup, p1-room24, p1-room30, rzx-p1- x18).
$9C05 b DeathShards 6 ; The shards' 9 paths: X, Y step pairs, read by DeathAnimation
$9C3B c SaveRestart ; A restart marker (cell $07) under Rex: save Rex's place, room and facing as the restart point, a chime
> Only when RexX & 7 = 2 (Rex centred on the marker) and the point differs from the saved one. The marker character is animated by AnimateRestart $A5B7.
> Witness: L1 1199 (c1, p1-cursor, p1-define, p1-kempston, p1-room24, p1-room30, rzx-p1- x26).
$9C45 RestartCompare ; the saved point differs?
$9C76 c LifeLost ; The end of a death: one life less; Rex back at the restart point, or the game over
> Lives $A063 - 1; ShowLives; Rex at RestartX/Y $A059/$A05A in RestartRoom $A05B, the shield off, the motion cleared; Materialise $9D1F and JP MainLoop $9583 (the room is built again). Lives at -1: GameOver $9CBF.
