@module cells ; The cells under Rex: ladders, restart markers, the shield recharger, the weapon stations
@about CellsUnderRex reads the grid under Rex's feet (RexCellPtr $A019 + $60, + $61). A ladder or lift ($12) stops his fall and lifts him; a restart marker ($07) saves the restart point; the recharger ($08) gives a unit of shield a pass; the four weapon stations ($0D double fire, $0A laser, $0B multiple, $0C spray) give the weapon and show its panel once.
$9F5F c CellsUnderRex ; Test the cells under Rex and act: lift, restart marker, recharger, weapon stations
> Witness: L1 16633 (c1, p1-code, p1-cursor, p1-define, p1-gameover, p1-kempston, p1-poke41241, p1-rooms238, p1-shots, p1-speedup, p1-room x5, rzx-p1- x32).
$9F97 OnLadder ; a ladder or lift: no fall, Rex lifted
$9FB2 StationDouble ; the double fire station
$9FC1 StationLaser ; the laser station
$9FD0 StationMultiple ; the multiple station
$9FDF c StationSpray ; The spray station ($0C): GiveSpray $A79D and the SPRAY panel (SprayText $ABCA)
> Witness: L1 69 (rzx-p1- x5).
$9FEE c Recharge ; The recharger ($08): ShieldEnergy + 1 up to 99 while the shield is off, the recharge sound
> Witness: L1 990 (p1-speedup, rzx-p1- x18).

@module variables ; The game's variables
@about All the state of a game sits in $A012-$A0C3, zero in the tape image: NewGame $9498 sets each before play. The temporaries $A093-$A09A are shared by many routines (a routine's input or scratch); the sprite parameters $A0AF-$A0B2 are DrawSprite's inputs.
$A012 b Variables 16 ; The variables $A012-$A0C3 (178 bytes, all zero on the tape)
@var $A012 FireLatch ; 1 while fire is held (one shot a press for the slow weapons)
@var $A013 Weapon ; the weapon in use: 0 gun, 1 double fire, 2 laser, 3 multiple (drones), 4 spray
@var $A014 PowerLevel ; the weapon's power, 1-5 (the power bar; PowerGain never stores 6)
@var $A015 PowerBarPtr 2 ; the HUD address of the power bar's end
@var $A017 PassToggle ; flips every pass (the animations run every other pass)
@var $A018 PowerCount ; power pods towards the next power level
@var $A019 RexCellPtr 2 ; Rex's place in the room grid (CellPointer $A503)
@var $A01B ObjectCellPtr 2 ; the current object's place in the grid (ObjectCell $C72B)
@var $A01D RoomCellPtr 2 ; DrawRoom's grid pointer
@var $A020 ObjectListPtr 2 ; the room's object list (RoomObjectLists)
@var $A022 HumanPicture ; the human picture's offset by weapon (KillHumanPicture $CE67)
@var $A028 BoxX ; PrintBoxed: the box's column
@var $A029 BoxY ; PrintBoxed: the box's line
@var $A02A BoxWidth ; PrintBoxed: the box's width
@var $A02B BoxHeight ; PrintBoxed: the box's height
@var $A02C SpawnLeft ; the room spawns from the left
@var $A02D SpawnRight ; the room spawns from the right
@var $A02E SpawnTop ; the room spawns from the top
@var $A02F SmartBombSteps ; the smart bomb's steps left (16)
@var $A030 SmartBombOn ; a smart bomb runs
@var $A031 SmartBombPtr 2 ; the next object to kill
@var $A033 SpriteMirror ; DrawSprite: bit 7 a fixed frame, SpritePicture, the frame list ignored (mirroring, through MirrorTable $AD5D, is A not 0 at the call)
@var $A034 SpritePicture 2 ; DrawSprite: the picture
@var $A038 ObjectHitCount ; the hits an object took
@var $A039 KillFlashPtr 2 ; the combo row cell lit by the latest hit ($5843 + 3 a hit; at rest $E9FF)
@var $A03B ComboCount ; kills in a row
