@module hud ; The HUD, the text printer, the numbers
@about The HUD fills the top three character rows: the score, lives, shield, weapons, bombs and the power bar. Texts are records [attribute][column][line in pixels] then characters ending with 0; PrintText prints one, PrintBoxed prints B records in a framed box (PanelBox $CE7B). Numbers go through ToDigits (five decimal digits, Digits $A0A6) and PrintDigits.
@about HudSweep is the bar that runs along the HUD's attribute row $582B: every 5 round trips it gets one narrower (SweepWidth $A067, 12 after ResetSweep $A133); when the width would drop to 0 ($A119-$A11B: DEC A, OR A, JP Z,RexDies) Rex dies. Room changes and deaths (RexDies) reset it. It stands still while the power pod's HUD flash runs (FadeStepIndex not $FF). p1-gameover lets it run down from width 2. The magazines' infinite-time POKE 43545,0 ($AA19) hits data in this release (ShardPaths); POKE 41241,0 (the DEC A at $A119 made a NOP) keeps the width.
$A0C4 c HudSweep ; One step of the HUD sweep (none while FadeStepIndex is not $FF); every 5 round trips one narrower; the width dropping to 0 kills Rex
