@module controls ; The controls: the self-modified key readers, the pause
@about Each control has a reader: IN A,(C) from a port, XOR ControlXor $A0AE ($FF for Kempston, whose bits are active high), BIT n,A; the zero flag set means pressed. The port and the BIT opcode are operands inside the readers, written by the setters ($A46A-$A4CE) when the menu's choice is made (DEFINE, Kempston, Cursor or Sinclair). The tape's defaults: fire O ($DFFE bit 1), left Q ($FBFE bit 0), right W ($FBFE bit 1), up I ($DFFE bit 2), down J ($BFFE bit 3).
