@module codepanel ; The end of part 1: the access code for part 2
@about Room exit 99 (the lift out of the complex) ends part 1 at CodePanel. The code is 16 digits that carry the game into part 2, in the places 0 double fire, 1 score thousands, 2 spray, 3 lives, 4 laser, 5 score hundreds, 6 multiple, 7 score units, 8 shield units, 9 score tens, 10 bombs, 11 shield tens, 12 score ten-thousands, each written 9 - digit; 13-15 the checksum's units, hundreds and tens (the sum of the 13 shown digits). The panel shows CODE: and the digits, waits for fire and starts a new game.
$A7CE c CodePanel ; The end of part 1: the CODE panel with the access code, then a new game
> Reached only from ChangeRoom $C95A when the exit leads to room 99. The digits go into CodeText $A884 at the places $A88C-$A89B. No stage 1 recording reached it; p1-code does (room 31's exit to 99, the panel shown, fire, a new game in room 0).
> Witness: L1 1 (p1-code).
$A84F CodeDigitsLoop ; each digit: 9 - digit, the checksum summed
$A884 b CodeText 8 ; The CODE panel: [attribute 6][column 6][line $50] "CODE:" and 16 places for the digits, 0
@res texts/rex1-code.bin
$A88C CodeDigits ; the 16 places: 0 double fire, 1 score thousands, 2 spray, 3 lives, 4 laser, 5 score hundreds, 6 multiple, 7 score units, 8 shield units, 9 score tens, 10 bombs, 11 shield tens, 12 score ten-thousands, each written 9 - digit; 13-15 the checksum's units, hundreds and tens (the sum of the 13 shown digits)
