@module tables ; The tables: bullet paths, key names, the scripted spawn, the shards, the texts, the screen lines, the mirror and shift tables, the rooms' objects and exits
$A9AF b BeamPath 2 ; The long bullet's path (bullet type 7, MoveBeam $B7FC): Y offset, picture pairs, then $1E and the beam's end records at BeamEnd $A9C9
$A9C9 BeamEnd ; the beam's last frames
$A9CC b KeyNames 8 ; The key characters of the 40 keys in the order of KeyPorts $E0E0 (CAPS as "-", ENTER "+", SYMBOL "."; key 0 also shows as "-"): DEFINE echoes them
> ScanKey $DBAE indexes it by half-row x 5 + bit. "1"-"5" are the last half-row; SPACE and H are refused (the smart bomb and pause keys).
$A9F4 b ScriptSpawn 5 ; The scripted spawn of rooms 2, 3, 4, 6 and 20: $1E then records [kind $85/$83/$84][X $E8][Y $12][delay 8], $FF ends
$AA0E b ShardPaths 16 ; The explosion's six shards (BlowUp $BD6B): 8 X, Y offset pairs each, $FF ends
$AA6E b ShardPictures 8 ; The explosion shards' pictures, 8 bytes each (DrawShard $BF66)
$AAAE b GameTexts 16 ; The game's text records: [attribute][column][line] text, 0
> PhaseOneText (3 records: PHASE ONE:PROCEED / ON FOOT THROUGH / UNDERGROUND COMPLEX), GameOverText, HiScoreText, HumansKilledText, PressFireText (2: PRESS FIRE / TO BEGIN), the bonus panels (SPEED UP, SHIELD LOSS, 1000 BONUS, ENERGY LOSS, 100 RAPID SHOTS) and the weapon panels, each after a flag byte that keeps it to one showing (DOUBLE FIRE, LASER, MULTIPLE, SPRAY). A ":" prints as "-" in the font.
@res texts/rex1-game.bin
$AAED GameOverText ; GAME OVER
$AAFA HiScoreText ; HI:SCORE 0000000
$AB0E HumansKilledText ; HUMANS KILLED:00000
$AB25 PressFireText ; PRESS FIRE / TO BEGIN
$AB41 BonusTexts ; the bonus panels, 19 bytes each: SPEED UP
$AB54 ShieldLossText ; SHIELD LOSS
$AB67 BonusPointsText ; 1000 BONUS
$AB7A EnergyLossText ; ENERGY LOSS
$AB8D RapidShotsText ; 100 RAPID SHOTS
$ABA0 DoubleFireText ; the flag (shown once), then DOUBLE FIRE
$ABB1 LaserText ; flag, LASER
$ABBC MultipleText ; flag, MULTIPLE
$ABCA SprayText ; flag, SPRAY
$ABD5 PixelMasks ; $80, $40, ... $01: a pixel's mask by X & 7
$ABDD w ScreenLineTable 8 ; The screen address of each of the 192 pixel lines (PrintChar, PrintDigits, PanelBox, DrawCharBlock)
$AC0D ScreenLines ; line 24 on: the play area's 168 lines, BufferToScreen's list
$AD5D b MirrorTable 16 ; Each byte with its bits reversed: DrawMirrored $B2C1 draws a picture facing left through it
$AE5D b ShiftFrames 8 ; The pictures' frame lists: 8 offsets each, one a pixel phase (X & 7), into a pre-shifted picture
> ShiftFrames ($00 $00 $30 $30 $60 $60 $90 $90: a 3 x 16 picture shifted every 2 pixels) for Rex and most objects; ShiftFrames2 $AE65 Rex jumping; $AE6D, $AE75, $AE7D, $AE85 the other sizes.
$AE65 ShiftFrames2
$AE6D ShiftFrames3
$AE75 ShiftFrames4
$AE7D ShiftFrames5
$AE85 ShiftFrames6
$AE8D AnimFramesA ; characters 252-255 on the passes with PassToggle 0: 4 x 8 bytes
$AEAD AnimFramesB ; characters 252-255 on the other passes: 4 x 8 bytes
$AECD b RoomObjectLists 16 ; The rooms' object lists: a header [spawn sides: bit 7 top, 6 right, 5 left][spawn period][spawn kind] (ReadExits $C8EF), then up to 16 records [kind][X][Y] (MakeObjects $CB52), $FF ends
@res rooms/rex1-objects.bin
$B133 b RoomExits 6 ; The exits of the rooms 0-34: up, right, down, left (0 none, 99 the end of part 1), then the word of the room's object list
> ReadExits $C8EF reads Room x 6. Room 0's record has no exits but room 1 to the right; the game starts in room 0.
@res rooms/rex1-exits.bin

@module render ; The renderer: the back buffer, the sprites, the animated cells
@about The play area is drawn in a back buffer of 32-byte lines ($E800 + 32 x line; the play's 168 lines are $EB00-$FFFF) and copied to the screen once a pass (BufferToScreen $A28A). ClearBuffer empties it with PUSH; DrawSprite ORs a pre-shifted picture into it (width and height written into its own loop operands), DrawMirrored the same through MirrorTable for a picture facing left.
