@module sound ; The sound: the AY effects
@about All the game's sound but the explosion's crackle (DrawShard $BF66, the beeper bit) is the AY: SoundWrite puts register D = E through $FFFD / $BFFD. No routine tests for an AY: on a 48K Spectrum without one the writes go to no device and the game plays silent but for the crackle (see work/stage2/NOTES.md, 48K / 128K).
@about An effect is a descriptor (SfxGun $D763 ...): [channel 1-3][noise flag: 0 a tone, else noise][steps][volume x 16][period word], then the steps, 3 bytes each: [count][period change, signed][volume change]. StartSfx copies it into its channel's 8 bytes at Channels $D832 ($FF free) and sets the mixer ($D855); SoundStep, called twice a pass, moves each channel one step (ChannelStep) and writes its tone and volume.
$D5AE c SoundReset ; The channels free, the mixer $38 (tones on, noise off), silence
> Witness: L1 84 (c1, p1-code, p1-cursor, p1-define, p1-kempston, p1-rooms238, p1-speedup, p1-room x5, rzx-p1- x30).
$D5D7 c SoundSilence ; The three volumes (registers 8-10) to 0
> Witness: L1 52036 (c1, p1-code, p1-cursor, p1-define, p1-gameover, p1-kempston, p1-rooms238, p1-speedup, p1-room x5, rzx-p1- x30).
