@module menu ; The title, the menu, DEFINE KEYS, the roll call
@about TitleMenu shows the title screen (loaded with the code at $E4FF and copied to the screen), prints the menu (SELECT 1:DEFINE 2:KEMPSTON 3:CURSOR 4:SINCLAIR) and, while it waits, rolls through the enemies with their names and scores (RollCallTexts $DC26, RollCallSprites $E067). A key 1-4 chooses the controls and asks to confirm (Y or N; N goes back to the menu). DEFINE asks for UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT and FIRE; each key is read by ScanKey and written into the reader's port and BIT operands.
@about The title screen's bytes, the roll call's pictures and the key table are needed only here: after the menu GameEntry clears $E4FF-$E7FE for the attribute shadow, and the room grid ($E19F-$E4FE) is built over the roll call's pictures. The menu copies the explosion picture ExplosionPicture $E336 to $6018 first, so it survives.
$DAC0 c TitleMenu ; The title and menu: the title on, the menu text, the roll call, the keys 1-4
> Witness: L1 1 (c1).
$DB11 MenuLoop ; the menu's wait: keys 1-4, the roll call
@isub $DB00 LD HL,RollCallSprites-12
$DB6E c RollCallRestart ; The roll call from its first sprite again (HL = RollCallSprites), then RollCallText
> TitleMenu's loop falls in here when the next sprite record is the list's $FF. Run by menu-rollcall (the menu left alone for 5310 frames, every enemy shown once). c1 also reads these bytes as data in play (frames 18550-20469; the reader is not identified).
> Witness: L1 1 (menu-rollcall).
$DB71 c RollCallText ; The next enemy's name and score (2 text records), the next record; at the list's end RollCallTextStart
> Witness: L1 14 (c1, menu-rollcall).
$DB85 c RollCallTextStart ; The names from the first again (IX = RollCallTexts), then RollCallNext
> Reached at the list's end. Run by menu-rollcall (the menu left alone for 5310 frames).
> Witness: L1 1 (menu-rollcall).
$DB89 c RollCallNext ; Keep the text pointer, back to the menu loop
> Witness: L1 14 (c1, menu-rollcall).
$DB90 RollCallTitle
$DB96 c ShowTitle ; The title screen ($E4FF) to the screen, the menu's attribute box
> Witness: L1 18 (c1, menu-rollcall, p1-cursor, p1-define, p1-kempston, rzx-p1-00000).
$DBAE c ScanKey ; DEFINE: wait for a key not SPACE, not H and not taken; its port into DefinePort, its BIT opcode into DefineBit, its character in A
